# Liquid Glass Design Rules

## Core Principles
- Glass belongs ONLY to navigation/chrome layer (tab bars, toolbars, sidebars, modals, popovers, FABs)
- NEVER apply glass to content (articles, feeds, table cells, list items)
- NEVER stack glass on glass — use flat fills for subdivisions
- Concentric radii: inner radius = outer radius − padding

## Base Glass Surface CSS
```css
.glass-surface {
  position: relative;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(180%) contrast(108%);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(180%) contrast(108%);
  box-shadow: 0 8px 32px -4px rgba(0,0,0,0.12), inset 0 1px 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.6);
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: 24px;
  isolation: isolate;
  contain: layout paint;
  transform: translateZ(0);
}
```

## Specular Border (::before)
Use `mask-composite: exclude` technique. NEVER use `border-image` with `border-radius`.

## Mandatory Fallbacks (include ALL):
- `@media (prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce)` → solid bg, no backdrop-filter
- `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` → no transitions
- `@media (prefers-contrast: more)` → 2px solid borders, no shadows
- `@media (forced-colors: active)` → Canvas/CanvasText system colors

## Typography: min font-weight 500, min 16px body. No mix-blend-mode on text.
## Performance: max 1 backdrop-filter on mobile. No will-change: backdrop-filter.
## Animation: use CSS linear() spring curves. No JS animation libraries needed.

